# Vite dev-mode defaults for `moon run compass-ui:dev` against a local
# `devenv up` backend. Vite loads this file automatically in dev (never in a
# build), so the dev task needs no env block of its own — and the file doubles
# as the in-repo documentation of which VITE_COMPASS_* keys the UI requires
# (src/live/connection.ts).
#
# Checked in deliberately: every value here is a loopback address, not a
# secret. Anything machine-specific belongs in `.env.local`, which Vite loads
# last (so it wins) and which is gitignored.

# These same two keys also parameterize a BUILD (not just the dev server): a
# previewable/production bundle is built by running `moon run compass-ui:build`
# (or `bunx vite build`) with VITE_COMPASS_BASE_URL + VITE_COMPASS_TOKEN set in
# the environment — Vite inlines each into `dist/` as a string literal, so one
# bundle boots against whatever door+bearer it was built with (an isolated
# PR-preview environment, a staging door, a local dogfood door). This file is
# NOT read by a build (Vite loads .env.development only in dev), so a build's
# door+bearer come from the build-time environment (process env, plus any
# tracked-free `.env`/`.env.local`/`.env.production` — all kept untracked by the
# env-secrecy gate), never these `.env.development` loopback defaults; supply
# them at build time.
# The preview-build gate (src/preview-build.test.ts) pins that a configured
# build actually bakes them in.

# The loopback gRPC-Web dev door compass-server binds under `devenv up`
# (devenv.nix:131 — `--dev-http 127.0.0.1:<devhttp>`).
#
# 50051 is devenv's allocation BASE, not a pin: `allocate` is documented as
# "Base port for auto-allocation (increments until free)"
# (devenv's src/modules/processes.nix) and the allocator scans upward
# from it unless `strict_ports` is
# set, which defaults false and is unset
# here. So if something already holds 50051, `devenv up` binds 50052+ and this
# URL points at nothing — the UI boots (both required vars are set) and fails at
# connect time instead. Check what `devenv up` reports and override
# VITE_COMPASS_BASE_URL in `.env.local` if it drifted.
VITE_COMPASS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:50051

# VITE_COMPASS_TOKEN is deliberately UNSET. The dev door is no-auth: it
# ambient-attributes every request to the bootstrap admin (go/server/serve.go:
# 254-262) and admin-gates the privileged RPCs ahead of that. Setting a real
# bearer here would put a live credential in a tracked file for no gain — the
# dev door ignores it. connection.ts normalizes absent/blank to `undefined`,
# which is exactly the no-auth client this door wants.

# There is deliberately NO caller-id env var: the UI learns the caller's own
# account id from the server via the compass.v1 WhoAmI RPC right after the
# transport is up (src/live/client.ts resolveCaller), so nothing to set here.
